---
import FeatureCard from '../../components/FeatureCard.astro';
import GuestQuote from '../../components/GuestQuote.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import TextSection from '../../components/TextSection.astro';
import { closures, formatPhone, mailHref, openingHours, price, site, telHref } from '../../data/facts.ts';
import { UI } from '../../data/ui.ts';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import '../../styles/pages/en/index.css';

const locale = 'en';
const text = UI[locale];
---

<Page
  locale={locale}
  page="home"
  title="Hotel Lärchenwald – a family hotel in Sils im Engadin"
  description="A family-run hotel by the larch forest above Lake Sils: quiet rooms panelled in stone pine, Engadin cooking and walks from the door. Ask us for a room."
>
  <Hero eyebrow="Sils im Engadin · 1,809 m above sea level" title="Quiet days between the larches and the lake">
    <p class="lede">
      Hotel Lärchenwald stands at the entrance to the Fex valley, ten minutes on foot from Lake Sils. For three
      generations the Clalüna family has welcomed guests here who come for the silence, good food and long walks.
    </p>
    <p><a class="button" href={mailHref(site.email)}>Ask for a room</a></p>
    <p>Or call us on <a href={telHref(site.phone)}>{formatPhone(site.phone)}</a></p>
  </Hero>

  <TextSection>
    <h2>A house with a history</h2>
    <p>
      The house was built in 1926 as a guesthouse for summer visitors, and it is a family business to this day. The 24
      rooms are panelled in Swiss stone pine, the soapstone stove of those early years still stands in the parlour, and
      in summer you sit on the terrace under old larches.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep things simple: a good bed, honest cooking and time for our guests. We will gladly bring a television to
      your room if you wish, and there is Wi-Fi throughout the house.
    </p>
  </TextSection>

  <TextSection>
    <h2>What awaits you here</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <FeatureCard title="Rooms looking into the Fex valley">
        <p>
          Single, double and family rooms in stone pine, each with a balcony and a view of the lake or of the Fex
          valley. The breakfast buffet, with bread from the village and Engadin mountain cheese, is included in the
          price.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Double room from {price('room-double', locale)} per night</strong></p>
      </FeatureCard>
      <FeatureCard title="Engadin cooking">
        <p>
          In the evening our chef, Reto Caduff, cooks a menu of four courses: barley soup, capuns (dumplings wrapped in
          chard leaves), game from the valley and the nut tart of the Engadin, baked to his grandmother’s recipe.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Evening menu {price('dinner-menu', locale)} per person</strong></p>
      </FeatureCard>
      <FeatureCard title="Walks from the front door">
        <p>
          The path into the Fex valley starts behind the house, and the Furtschellas cable car is five minutes away. In
          winter the cross-country ski trail runs past the hotel.
        </p>
      </FeatureCard>
      <FeatureCard title="Time to yourself">
        <p>
          A small sauna that looks into the forest, a library with an open fire and a garden with deckchairs. Your dog
          is welcome here too.
        </p>
      </FeatureCard>
    </div>
  </TextSection>

  <TextSection>
    <h2>What our guests say</h2>
    <GuestQuote source="Margaret and Alan H. from Edinburgh, guests in October">
      <p>
        “We came for three nights and stayed for eight. The silence, the larches turning gold, and the best barley soup
        we have ever had: we will be back.”
      </p>
    </GuestQuote>
  </TextSection>

  <TextSection>
    <h2>Getting here and contact</h2>
    <p>
      You reach Sils with the Rhaetian Railway as far as St. Moritz, and from there by bus in twenty minutes. The stop
      “Sils/Segl Maria, Posta” is five minutes on foot from the hotel. If you wish, we will meet you there and carry
      your luggage.
    </p>
    <address>
      {site.name}<br>
      {site.address.street}<br>
      {site.address.postalCode}
      {site.address.locality}<br>
      {text.phone}{text.colon} <a href={telHref(site.phone)}>{formatPhone(site.phone)}</a><br>
      {text.email}{text.colon} <a href={mailHref(site.email)}>{site.email}</a>
    </address>
    <dl>
      {openingHours(locale, text.everyDay).map((row) => (
        <>
          <dt>{text.reception}</dt>
          <dd>
            {row.days}, {row.hours} {text.hoursSuffix}
          </dd>
        </>
      ))}
      {closures(locale).map((range) => (
        <>
          <dt>{text.closed}</dt>
          <dd>{range}</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </TextSection>
</Page>
